      "status": "accepted",
      "explanation": "The original kernel builds a std::string by repeatedly concatenating one character per iteration, which causes O(n^2) allocations and copies. By eliminating the temporary string and computing the character and checksum directly while iterating over the generated values, we reduce memory allocations and improve cache locality. This preserves the exact numeric result for all inputs, keeping observable behavior unchanged while yielding a noticeable speedup, especially for larger n.",
